"D", "text": "Herpes simplex virus"}, {"label": "E", "text": "West Nile virus"}], "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_T84261\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">C</mark>ommon causes of eosinophilia</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Peripheral</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Helminth infection</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Allergen exposure</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Drug reaction</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Rheumatic disease</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Malignancy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Meningeal</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Helminth infection (eg, angiostrongyliasis)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Fungal infection (eg, coccidioidomycosis)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Drug reaction</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Hematologic malignancy (eg, Hodgkin lymphoma)</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This patient has a severe headache, nausea, and an elevated eosinophil count in the cerebrospinal fluid, indicating <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">eosinophilic meningitis</strong>, a condition most often caused by <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Angiostrongylus cantonensis</strong></em> infection.\u00a0 Humans are incidental hosts and typically acquire the helminth by eating contaminated mollusks or snails while in <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Southeast Asia</strong> or the Pacific Islands.\u00a0 Eosinophilic meningitis can also be caused by other helminths (eg, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Gnathostoma</em>, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Baylisascaris</em>) or, less commonly, by fungi (eg, coccidioidomycosis), leukoproliferative disorders (eg, Hodgkin lymphoma), or an adverse drug reaction.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Eosinophils are of the granulocyte lineage (along with basophils and neutrophils), and the majority of total body eosinophils are in tissue (eg, spleen, lymph nodes, thymus, digestive tract).\u00a0 However, polyclonal <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">expansion of peripheral eosinophils</strong> can occur due to release of <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">IL-5</strong> by T<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">H</sub>2 lymphocytes and innate lymphoid cells in response to <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">helminth infection</strong>, <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">allergens</strong>, <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">drugs</strong>, or rheumatic disease; IL-5 may also be constitutively expressed by solid organ <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">malignancies</strong>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Cryptococcus neoformans</em> can rarely cause eosinophilic meningitis.\u00a0 However, cryptococcal infections primarily occur in those with profound immunocompromise (eg, AIDS) and typically present with subacute manifestations (eg, fever and headache over 1-2 weeks).\u00a0 This patient who is otherwise healthy and recently traveled to Asia is far more likely to have <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Angiostrongylus cantonensis</em>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice C)</strong>\u00a0 <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Mycobacterium tuberculosis</em> is possible in a patient who travels extensively to endemic areas.\u00a0 Although tubercular meningitis may occur, it causes lymphocyte-predominant meningitis; eosinophilic meningitis is not seen.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice D)</strong>\u00a0 Herpes simplex virus can cause encephalitis due to infection of the temporal lobe.\u00a0 Patients usually present with fever, focal neurologic deficit, and/or seizure.\u00a0 Dramatically elevated erythrocytes (due to cerebral microhemorrhage), not eosinophils, are typically seen on cerebrospinal fluid analysis.\u00a0 In addition, brain imaging generally reveals temporal lobe abnormalities.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice E)</strong>\u00a0 West Nile virus is usually marked by a lymphocyte-predominant meningitis; profound cerebrospinal fluid eosinophilia is uncommon.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Eosinophilic meningitis is most often due to helminth infection (eg, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Angiostrongylus</em>).\u00a0 Peripheral eosinophilia is largely mediated by the release of IL-5 in response to helminths, allergens, drugs, or rheumatic disease.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Eosinophilic meningitis is most often due to helminth infection (eg, Angiostrongylus ).  Peripheral eosinophilia is largely mediated by the release of IL-5 in response to helminths, allergens, drugs, or rheumatic disease.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b", "subject": "Microbiology", "system": "Infectious Diseases", "topic": "Angiostrongylus infection", "category": "Parasitic and helminthic infections", "peerCorrect": 56.0}